        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_1650"/>
        <dc:title>Pattern and synchrony of gene expression among sympatric marine microbial populations</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>SignificanceMicrobial communities regulate the cycling of energy and matter in the environment, yet how they respond to environmental change is not well-known. We describe here a day in the life of wild planktonic microbial species using robotic sampling coupled with genome-wide gene expression analysis. Our results showed that closely related populations, as well as very different bacterial and archaeal species, displayed remarkably similar time-variable synchronous patterns of gene expression over 2 d. Our results suggest that specific environmental cues may elicit cross-species coordination of gene expression among diverse microbial groups, potentially enabling multispecies coupling of metabolic activity.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2013-02-05</dc:date>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:libraryCatalog>Crossref</z:libraryCatalog>
