        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_2233"/>
        <dc:title>Simultaneous determination of dissolved organic carbon and total dissolved nitrogen in seawater by high temperature catalytic oxidation: conditions for precise shipboard measurements</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Appropriate conditions have been achieved for the accurate, rapid, and highly precise shipboard simultaneous determination of dissolved organic carbon and total dissolved nitrogen in seawater by high temperature catalytic oxidation. A nitrogen-specific Antek 705D chemiluminescence detector and a CO -specific LiCor Li6252 IRGA have been coupled 2 in-series with a Shimadzu TOC-5000 organic carbon analyser. Precision of both simultaneous measurements is F 1.5%, i.e. &quot;1 mmol C ly1 and &quot;0.3 mmol N ly1, respectively. Quality of analysis is not compromised by vibrations associated with ocean going research vessels. q 1998 Elsevier Science B.V. All rights reserved.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>11/1998</dc:date>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:shortTitle>Simultaneous determination of dissolved organic carbon and total dissolved nitrogen in seawater by high temperature catalytic oxidation</z:shortTitle>
        <z:libraryCatalog>DOI.org (Crossref)</z:libraryCatalog>
